=== ARTICLE: Overture - under the hood ===
[size=5][b]How Overture works[/b][/size]

This is the technical side of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109433]Overture[/url]. The mod page tells you what you see in game. This article says what happens behind it.

[size=4][b]The conversation[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Overture opens before the NPC's own dialogue, once per game day per person. It needs no hotkey, menu or spell.[/*]
[*]It is built on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport[/url], which keeps what your words did as the bond between you and runs the scene.[/*]
[*]Every NPC is one of four kinds of people, and each of the four ways of trying lands with exactly one kind.[/*]
[*]"Ask for a moment" appears only where the conversation can open: the same eight checks the conversation makes.[/*]
[*]The mod is Papyrus only. It has no native code.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]The R button and its menu[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]E stays the NPC's own talk. R, "Overture", opens the short menu: Try your luck, Follow me, Just talk, Later.[/*]
[*]The perk fragment record that tells the game which script to run must hold exactly the bytes the game expects. For a while it held one byte too many, so R, Follow me and "Ask for a moment" did nothing. That is fixed.[/*]
[*]Extended Dialogue Interface shows the NPC's response line, not your prompt, and drops an option with an empty response. That hid "Try your luck" and every silent option (Linger, taking their hand), which have no spoken words. That is fixed too.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Voices[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]236 NPC lines in 11 voices, 5,199 voice files in all, plus two voices of your own, a woman's and a man's, never a copy of any actor.[/*]
[*]Every option on the wheel comes in five versions, and each conversation picks one.[/*]
[*]Characters with their own actor answer in the closest voice we have, through Rapport, for that line only.[/*]
[*]Rapport finds a missing recording by looking for the loose file. That is why Overture's [font=Courier New]Sound/Voice/Overture.esp[/font] folder must stay loose and not be packed into an archive: packed lines go silent or borrow the wrong voice.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Follow me[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Someone who says "not here" follows you somewhere quieter. Anyone you've warmed up can be asked with "Follow me".[/*]
[*]They keep to their own place: anywhere in their town or settlement, never out of it, and about 60 m in the open.[/*]
[*]Two game hours without somewhere private, or you running off, and they head back. Once you're alone they speak first and the talk opens at the proposition.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Older Rapport[/b][/size]
With an older Rapport than 0.2.1, Overture still runs, without names, lovers or the narrator, and says so once. "Start now" in the MCM needs Rapport 0.2.2.
